# |AutoCCZ>: one CCZ state distilled from 8 T states, with the three routing pairs that make
# its Clifford fix-ups measurement bases (Gidney & Fowler 2019; the state FormalRV's Toffoli
# lowering consumes: compiler/lib/prog_to_qppm/ppmc.ml, auto_ccx).  The msccz place compiles
# exactly this (qccd/gadget/leaves/ccz.py, ring_circuit), every TSIR gate, reset and
# measurement naming the line it realises; its logic check runs it as a state vector.
#
# DISTILLATION, 8T -> CCZ on the [[8,3,2]] cube code.  Qubit k (0..7) is the cube vertex whose
# coordinates are the bits of k.  The code's |+++> is the uniform superposition over the
# Reed-Muller code RM(1,3), spanned by the all-ones word and the three faces {v : v_i = 0}; in
# row echelon form its pivots are {0, 1, 2, 4}.  T on the even vertices and T-dagger on the
# odd ones is logical CCZ.  Decoding with the same CNOT fan leaves pivot 0 entangled with the
# other three by X on all of them; three CNOTs from it undo that, and it is read in X.  The
# five detectors (pivot 0 in X, the non-pivots 3, 5, 6, 7 in Z) all 0 is the post-selection;
# any one T fault shows in them (distance 2: output error 28 p^2).  Qubits 1, 2, 4 then hold
# CCZ|+++>.
#
# ROUTING, six more ions (8..13): one pair per CZ fix-up of the Toffoli it will serve --
# (8, 9) for (b, t), (10, 11) for (a, t), (12, 13) for (a, b) -- each prepared as CZ|++> and
# CNOT-linked from its two state qubits, the first state qubit into the first of the pair.
# (Checked: FormalRV's own consumption of these nine sites is CCX(a, b, t) in all 4,096
# branches; with the links crossed it is not.)
#
# The nine outputs, in FormalRV's site order x y z s3 s4 s5 s6 s7 s8:
output 1 2 4 8 9 10 11 12 13

# every ion fresh
reset 0
reset 1
reset 2
reset 3
reset 4
reset 5
reset 6
reset 7
reset 8
reset 9
reset 10
reset 11
reset 12
reset 13

# encode |+++> in the cube code: the pivots in |+>, the fan of RM(1,3)'s echelon rows
H 0
H 1
H 2
H 4
CX 0 3
CX 0 5
CX 0 6
CX 1 3
CX 1 5
CX 1 7
CX 2 3
CX 2 6
CX 2 7
CX 4 5
CX 4 6
CX 4 7

# transversal T on the even vertices, T-dagger on the odd: logical CCZ
T 0
T_DAG 1
T_DAG 2
T 3
T_DAG 4
T 5
T 6
T_DAG 7

# decode with the same fan, in reverse
CX 4 7
CX 4 6
CX 4 5
CX 2 7
CX 2 6
CX 2 3
CX 1 7
CX 1 5
CX 1 3
CX 0 6
CX 0 5
CX 0 3

# pivot 0 is entangled with the outputs by X on all three: undo it, read it in X
CX 0 1
CX 0 2
CX 0 4
H 0

# the five detectors
measure 0
measure 3
measure 5
measure 6
measure 7

# routing pair (8, 9) for the fix-up (b, t): CZ|++>, linked from y = 2 and z = 4
H 8
CX 8 9
H 9
CX 2 8
CX 4 9

# routing pair (10, 11) for (a, t): linked from x = 1 and z = 4
H 10
CX 10 11
H 11
CX 1 10
CX 4 11

# routing pair (12, 13) for (a, b): linked from x = 1 and y = 2
H 12
CX 12 13
H 13
CX 1 12
CX 2 13
